[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1287","stub":{"id":"1287","section":"Duck Hole to mouth","altname":"","river":"Cold","difficulty":"IItoVplus","states":["USA-NYO"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"4.17","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"levelFT","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"108907","location":{"latitude":"44.1408996582031","longitude":"-74.1097030639648"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"114143","location":{"latitude":"44.1006011962891","longitude":"-74.3145980834961"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"24","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"101248548","title":null,"post_date":"2011-09-01 04:00:00+00","detail":"Adirondack Explorer reports that the Duck Hole Dam was breached in during Hurricane Irene. This may make the Cold much harder to catch, no pun intended.\n\nAccess the article here: http://adirondackexplorer.org/out-takes/2011/08/30/after-irene-where-can-you-hike/","user":{"name":"Eric Adsit"}}],"photos":[{"id":"DTWpHMPtVPrdc6nq02Uzk","ext":"jpg","post_id":"oJzb6g21X6SijyJNFjeDt","description":"<p>Check out Brian Page setting safety on river right. Pretty large rapid with holes deeper than a person.</p>","caption":"Millers Falls","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Charles Wygal","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/DTWpHMPtVPrdc6nq02Uzk","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/DTWpHMPtVPrdc6nq02Uzk"}},{"id":"EgfD26tOPCbZqVqENekI4","ext":"jpg","post_id":"oJzb6g21X6SijyJNFjeDt","description":"<p>If the water is above the base of the signs, you're in for a treat</p>","caption":"The Takeout","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Charles Wygal","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/EgfD26tOPCbZqVqENekI4","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/EgfD26tOPCbZqVqENekI4"}},{"id":"egCtCysPJWEDgdl2hTQkF","ext":"jpg","post_id":"oJzb6g21X6SijyJNFjeDt","description":"","caption":"Duck Hole Fire","poi_name":null,"subject":"A Vibe and a half","author":"Charles Wygal","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/egCtCysPJWEDgdl2hTQkF","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/egCtCysPJWEDgdl2hTQkF"}},{"id":"NkSMmjhS4Zd1ERWLisqX4","ext":"jpg","post_id":"oJzb6g21X6SijyJNFjeDt","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Charles Wygal","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-05-07T16:48:26.000Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T16:48:26.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/NkSMmjhS4Zd1ERWLisqX4","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/NkSMmjhS4Zd1ERWLisqX4"}},{"id":"AnBBDIdIZnJ1vehV6Q1yT","ext":"jpg","post_id":"oJzb6g21X6SijyJNFjeDt","description":"<p>Took the sneak river right. Huge hole in the middle. Picture doesn't do it justice</p>","caption":"Upper Raquette Falls","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Charles Wygal","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/AnBBDIdIZnJ1vehV6Q1yT","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/AnBBDIdIZnJ1vehV6Q1yT"}},{"id":"AtVlidk2HjXurjYrhh7dh","ext":"jpg","post_id":"oJzb6g21X6SijyJNFjeDt","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Charles Wygal","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/AtVlidk2HjXurjYrhh7dh","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/AtVlidk2HjXurjYrhh7dh"}},{"id":"Er8zctrVu84e6r2xtLRyw","ext":"jpg","post_id":"oJzb6g21X6SijyJNFjeDt","description":"<p>No clean lines through this. Huge boils and holes in the upper. With some fun looking class 4 below. To launch here would've been difficult so we put in around the corner where it is the final whitewater stretch.</p>","caption":"Lower Raquette Falls","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Charles Wygal","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/Er8zctrVu84e6r2xtLRyw","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/Er8zctrVu84e6r2xtLRyw"}},{"id":"XnPcmpDapJeJMDEkJ99i7","ext":"jpg","post_id":"oJzb6g21X6SijyJNFjeDt","description":"<p>Charles Wygal breaking up the slog with a smile to generate stoke</p>","caption":"Stoke on the 2+ mile portage","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Charles Wygal","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/XnPcmpDapJeJMDEkJ99i7","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/XnPcmpDapJeJMDEkJ99i7"}},{"id":"VaYbkuxqQ1qJ3ZGq6VH80","ext":"jpg","post_id":"oJzb6g21X6SijyJNFjeDt","description":"<p>A perfect camp site. Let us lighten our loads by not needing to bring tents. Plenty of lean to's along this stretch of river</p>","caption":"Duck Hole Lean To","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Charles Wygal","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/VaYbkuxqQ1qJ3ZGq6VH80","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/VaYbkuxqQ1qJ3ZGq6VH80"}},{"id":"Wwmpy7L36RbQbDFNgGwya","ext":"jpg","post_id":"oJzb6g21X6SijyJNFjeDt","description":"<p>After running into a canoe fisherman who gave beta about tons of brookies in the Preston Ponds I added the fly rod to the loadout. No fish for me though, would've been awesome to catch n cook some trout on the fire at camp. Western Daks have firepits at many of the lean-tos</p>","caption":"Fishin duck hole","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Charles Wygal","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/Wwmpy7L36RbQbDFNgGwya","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/Wwmpy7L36RbQbDFNgGwya"}},{"id":"l0NdeJoaPrwzYnN4962Z6","ext":"jpg","post_id":"oJzb6g21X6SijyJNFjeDt","description":"<p>Almost routed this blind. Langton hopped out to scout as I sat in an eddy and we made the right choice not to drop in. Tight techy slot which went, but then you would've had to get back out and scramble the rock jumble to get down to Duck Hole. Juice wasn't worth the squeeze. Langton styled this the best way</p>","caption":"Lower Preston to Duck Hole drop","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Charles Wygal","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/l0NdeJoaPrwzYnN4962Z6","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/l0NdeJoaPrwzYnN4962Z6"}},{"id":"KV08SPKqHJSqdi6vQpaND","ext":"jpg","post_id":"oJzb6g21X6SijyJNFjeDt","description":"<p>Final rapid of the Cold. Big bridge of the Northville Placid trail and a massive horizon line is the best visual indicator. Luckily the hiking trail follows the river right side of the rapid so portaging this was a breeze. It goes, but huge sticky holes plus loaded boats and a straight up fun not scary day had us all feeling like keepin it a low risk fun trip. From this point you're miles in the wilderness and first responders would be a day or 2 away.</p>","caption":"Millers Falls with the final hole under the bridge","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Charles Wygal","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","updated_at":"2025-05-07T16:48:27.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/KV08SPKqHJSqdi6vQpaND","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/KV08SPKqHJSqdi6vQpaND"}},{"id":"877517","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"877807","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/877517","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/877517"}},{"id":"877518","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"877808","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/877518","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/877518"}}],"detail":{"id":"1287","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"This is a long run and should either be done in one very long day, or as an overnighter.\n\nFrom the parking lot the put in is a 5 mile hike to Duck Hole Dam. The run starts with a mile of Class 4 followed by a short section of Class 5. This is followed by a Class 2-3 gorge.  8 miles downstream are two significant drops (and a lean-to if you choose to spend the night).  At the confluence with the Raquette go left (upstream) towards Long Lake.\n\nThe alternate takeout is to go downstream on the Raquette, run Raquette Falls, and take out at Axton Landing.\n\n**Eastern Adirondacks Reaches**\n\n[Ausable, E. Branch](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1238/) [Ausable, W. Branch (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1241/) [Ausable, W. Branch (2.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1239/) [Balm of Gilead Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/2996/)\n\n[Boquet (2.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1261/) [Boquet (3.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1262/) [Boquet, N. Branch](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1264/)[Boquet, S. Branch](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1263/)\n\n[Boreas (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1266/) [Branch, The (Boquet trib.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1441/) [Branch, The (Schroon trib.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1442/) [Cedar (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1280/)\n\n[Cedar (2.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1281/) [Cold](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1287/) [Deer Creek (Hudson Trib.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1184/)[Glen Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1309/)\n\n[Hague Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10876/) [Hudson (0.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10653/) [Hudson (1. Indian River to North River)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1321/) [Hudson (2. North River to Riparius)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1322/)\n\n[Hudson (3. Riparius to the Glen)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1323/) [Indian (Hudson trib.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1325/) [John's Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/2913/)[La Chute](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1335/)\n\n[Mettawee](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1343/)[Mill Creek (Essex County](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4251/))                    [Mill Creek (Hudson trib.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1346/) [North Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4303/)\n\n[Pike Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/10886/) [Poultney](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1383/)[Putnam Creek](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4253/) [Raquette (1.)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1385/)\n\n[Rock River](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1391/) [Schroon (North Hudson to Schroon Falls)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1422/) [Schroon (Starbuckville to Riverbank)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1423/)[Schroon (Warrensburg to Thurman Station)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1421/)\n\n[Squaw Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/3886/) [Styles Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4281/) [Thirteenth Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/1443/) [Trout brook (Schroon trib)](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/3284/)\n\n[West Mill Brook](https://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/detail/id/4314/)\n\n**[Google Map of New York Whitewater](https://www.google.com/maps/d/edit?mid=zjdnDE8H0TLg.kJnMWGapL4xk)**\n\n**[New York Whitewater Paddlers Facebook Group](https://www.facebook.com/groups/108070075877312/)**","averageGradient":"0","maxGradient":"0","length":"14.5","correlations":[{"reachID":"1287","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"levelFT","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"6","beginMediumRunnable":null,"begi